<div style="background-color: #1a5276; color: white; padding: 15px; text-align: center; border-radius: 8px; margin-bottom: 20px;">
    <h1 style="margin: 0;">Lesson Planner – Theme # I Need an Umbrella. – Lesson # 3</h1>
    <p style="margin: 5px 0 0 0; font-size: 1.1em;">Complete this planner five times per theme, once per lesson (Lesson 1 through Lesson 5).</p>
</div>

<table style="border: 1px dashed #333; border-collapse: collapse; width: 100%; margin: 10px 0;">
    <tbody>
        <tr>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px; width: 50%;"><b>Lesson #:</b> 3</td>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px; width: 50%;"><b>Skills Focus:</b> Speaking</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;"><b>Grade:</b> 4th Grade (CEFR: A1.2)</td>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;"><b>Scenario:</b> It's the Rainy Season</td>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;"><b>Theme:</b> I Need an Umbrella.</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;"><b>Date(s):</b> From ___ to ___</td>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;" colspan="2"><b>Learning Sequence Time:</b> 45–50 min</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;" colspan="3">
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Specific Objective:</b> Speaking: Engage in simple exchanges about personal interests.</p>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Learning Outcome:</b> Speaking: Can narrate, using basic descriptive phrases, a simple current event related to rainy weather (e.g., 'It is raining today, and I am jumping in puddles.'). Can engage in simple exchanges about activities during rainy weather with peers (e.g., 'What do you like to do when it rains?' 'I like to read inside.'). Can collaborate with classmates to give a short presentation on rainy day activities they like to do (e.g., 'We bring umbrellas and boots when it rains.').</p>
            </td>
        </tr>
    </tbody>
</table>

<h2 style="color: #1a5276; margin-top: 30px;">The Six Action-Oriented Approach (AOA) Lesson Stages</h2>
<table style="border: 1px dashed #333; border-collapse: collapse; width: 100%; margin: 10px 0;">
    <thead>
        <tr>
            <th style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px; background-color: #f2f2f2; color: #1a5276; width: 35%;">Stage & Description</th>
            <th style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px; background-color: #f2f2f2; color: #1a5276; width: 45%;">Activities & Teacher Actions</th>
            <th style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px; background-color: #f2f2f2; color: #1a5276; width: 20%;">Estimated Date and Time</th>
        </tr>
    </thead>
    <tbody>
        <tr>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>STAGE 1 — Warm-up / Pre-task</b></p>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;">Engagement, Modeling and Clarification</p>
            </td>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Warm-up:</b> The teacher holds up flashcards or realia (e.g., a small umbrella, rain boot, picture of a puddle). Teacher asks, "What is this?" and elicits the vocabulary words previously introduced. Students repeat chorally and individually. Teacher says, "It is raining! What do we need?" and prompts students to say "umbrella," "raincoat," "boots."</p>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Modeling:</b> The teacher models target phrases and pronunciation. "When it rains, I need an umbrella." "I wear my boots." Teacher exaggerates the /r/ sound in 'rain' and 'raincoat' and the /p/ sound in 'puddle'. Teacher demonstrates blending: "Listen: /sk/ /aɪ/ makes 'sky'." "Listen: /m/ /ʌdi/ makes 'muddy'." Teacher asks students to repeat. Teacher then models simple sentences for sharing experiences: "I like to read when it rains." "I like to puddle-jump."</p>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Clarification (CCQs):</b></p>
                <ul style="margin: 0; padding-left: 20px;">
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">"Do we need an umbrella when it's sunny?" (No.)</li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">"Can we splash in puddles when it's dry?" (No.)</li>
                </ul>
            </td>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;">[5-7 minutes]</p>
            </td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>STAGE 2 — Presentation</b></p>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;">Input of new language/content connected to Scenario: "It's the Rainy Season."</p>
            </td>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Material:</b> A short, illustrated dialogue between two friends (Ana and Leo) discussing rainy day activities and needs.</p>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Dialogue Example:</b></p>
                <ul style="margin: 0; padding-left: 20px;">
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;"><b>Ana:</b> "Look! It is raining today."</li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;"><b>Leo:</b> "Oh no! I need my umbrella. What do you need, Ana?"</li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;"><b>Ana:</b> "I need my raincoat and boots. I like to puddle-jump!"</li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;"><b>Leo:</b> "I don't like to splash. I like to read inside when it is rainy."</li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;"><b>Ana:</b> "My boots are muddy now. The sky is gloomy."</li>
                </ul>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;">The teacher reads the dialogue aloud, pointing to the pictures. Students listen.</p>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Communicative Competence:</b> Talking about rainy weather: 'I need an umbrella.' Sharing experiences: 'I wear my boots when it rains.' 'I am wearing my boots because it is raining.' Narrating current events related to weather: Using the present continuous tense (e.g., 'It is raining. I like puddle-jumping.').</p>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Comprehension tasks:</b></p>
                <ul style="margin: 0; padding-left: 20px;">
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">Teacher asks: "Who needs an umbrella?" (Leo)</li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">Teacher asks: "What does Ana like to do?" (Puddle-jump.)</li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">Teacher asks: "Is it sunny or rainy in the dialogue?" (Rainy.)</li>
                </ul>
            </td>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;">[8-10 minutes]</p>
            </td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>STAGE 3 — Preparation / Practice</b></p>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;">Accuracy focus on Speaking</p>
            </td>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Communicative Skill & Content:</b> Present simple for routines (e.g., 'I wear my boots when it rains.'), present continuous for current events (e.g., 'It is raining today.'), WH-questions (What do you need? What do you like to do?). Vocabulary: puddle, umbrella, raincoat, boots, splash, pour, need, want, wet, rainy, muddy, sky, gloomy. Pronunciation: /r/ and /p/ sounds. Phonemic awareness: Spelling 'raincoat', 'muddy', 'sky'.</p>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Detailed Procedure:</b></p>
                <ul style="margin: 0; padding-left: 20px;">
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;"><b>1. Controlled Oral Sentence Completion:</b> Teacher displays incomplete sentences on the board or projector with picture prompts (e.g., "When it rains, I need a (picture of umbrella)."). Students complete the sentence orally in chorus, then individually. Teacher encourages correct pronunciation of target words.</li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;"><b>2. Semi-controlled Pair Chain Drill:</b> Students work in pairs. Partner A asks, "What do you wear when it rains?" Partner B responds, "I wear my (boots/raincoat)." Then Partner B asks, "What do you like to do when it rains?" Partner A responds, "I like to (read inside/puddle-jump)." They practice using present simple and specific vocabulary. Teacher circulates, listening for accuracy and providing feedback on pronunciation and grammar.</li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;"><b>3. Guided Q&A with Visuals:</b> Teacher shows various pictures of rainy day scenarios or items (e.g., kids splashing in puddles, someone holding an umbrella, a muddy street). In pairs, students take turns asking and answering WH-questions based on the pictures. For example, "What is she doing?" (She is puddle-jumping.) "What do you see in the sky?" (I see a cloud. It is gloomy.) Teacher prompts students to use present continuous for actions happening now and present simple for preferences.</li>
                </ul>
            </td>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;">[15-17 minutes]</p>
            </td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>STAGE 4 — Performance / Production</b></p>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;">Communicative task where students USE the language in a realistic scenario: "It's the Rainy Season."</p>
            </td>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Task Format:</b> Small group presentation.</p>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Description:</b> Students work in groups of 3-4. Each group discusses and chooses 2-3 favorite activities they like to do when it rains, and 2-3 items they need/wear. They prepare a short, simple presentation (1-2 minutes) to share with the class. They must use sentences like, "When it rains, we like to [activity]." "We bring [item] when it rains." "It is raining now, and we are [doing activity]." Teacher encourages them to use target vocabulary (puddle, umbrella, raincoat, boots, splash, pour, need, want, wet, rainy, muddy, gloomy, sky) and grammar (present simple, present continuous, WH-questions for peer interaction). They should also focus on clear pronunciation of /r/ and /p/ sounds. Each group presents their ideas to the class.</p>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Connection to Theme:</b> The presentations directly address the theme "I Need an Umbrella." by focusing on items and activities related to rainy weather.</p>
            </td>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;">[10-12 minutes]</p>
            </td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>STAGE 5 — Assessment / Post-task</b></p>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;">Formative assessment strategy.</p>
            </td>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Assessment Task:</b> Observe students during their group presentations (Stage 4).</p>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Evaluation Criteria (Teacher Observation Checklist):</b></p>
                <ul style="margin: 0; padding-left: 20px;">
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;"><b>Intelligible pronunciation:</b> Clear production of /r/ and /p/ sounds. (Yes/No/Needs work)</li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;"><b>Use of target vocabulary:</b> (e.g., umbrella, boots, puddle-jump, rainy, muddy). (Used 3+ / Used 1-2 / Not used)</li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;"><b>Use of grammar:</b> Present simple and present continuous. (Mostly correct / Some errors / Many errors)</li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;"><b>Clarity & Fluency:</b> Messages are understandable, reasonable pace. (Clear / Mostly clear / Difficult to understand)</li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;"><b>Collaboration:</b> Participated actively in the group task. (Yes / Partially / No)</li>
                </ul>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Student Self-Assessment / Exit Ticket:</b> Students answer the following questions on a small slip of paper:</p>
                <ul style="margin: 0; padding-left: 20px;">
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">"What is one new word you used today when speaking about rainy weather?"</li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">"What is one thing you can say in English about what you like to do when it rains?"</li>
                </ul>
            </td>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;">[5-7 minutes]</p>
            </td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>STAGE 6 — Reflection</b></p>
            </td>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Student self-reflection prompt:</b></p>
                <ul style="margin: 0; padding-left: 20px;">
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">"What part of speaking in English today was easy for you?"</li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">"What part was difficult, and what can you do to improve?"</li>
                </ul>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Teacher reflection:</b> Most students successfully engaged in simple exchanges about rainy weather activities, showing good use of the present simple and some use of the present continuous. The pronunciation practice for /r/ and /p/ needs continuous reinforcement. Group presentations allowed for good collaboration and fluency practice. Some students struggled with forming complete sentences in the present continuous. I will prepare more sentence frames for the next lesson to support their writing.</p>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Connection to next lesson:</b> In Lesson 4, students will transition from speaking about rainy day activities to writing about them, focusing on sentence construction and short descriptive paragraphs using the vocabulary and grammar practiced today.</p>
            </td>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;">[3-4 minutes]</p>
            </td>
        </tr>
    </tbody>
</table>